---
import { VIDEO } from '../consts';
---

<section class="video-section" id="watch" aria-labelledby="watch-heading">
  <h2 id="watch-heading">Watch: StripChat Free Tokens Safety Guide</h2>
  <p>
    Before you read on, this 60-second YouTube Short from the {VIDEO.publisherName}
    channel covers the same ground as this guide: why “hack” and “mod APK”
    token offers are almost always traps, which warning signs to look for, and
    the safe steps you can take instead. If you only have a minute, watch the
    video — then use the written guide below for the details and checklists.
  </p>
  <div class="video-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe
          src={VIDEO.embedUrl}
          title="YouTube Shorts: Stripchat hack mod warning — what to check before you click (2026/2027)"
          loading="lazy"
          allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
          allowfullscreen
          referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"></iframe>
      </div>
      <p class="video-caption">
        Short video: the red flags of “Stripchat hack” and “mod APK” token offers.
        Video by {VIDEO.publisherName} on YouTube.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="video-summary">
      <h3>What the video covers</h3>
      <p>
        The video is a consumer-warning piece about websites that claim to
        “hack” StripChat tokens or install a “mod” for unlimited tokens.
        According to its creator, its main points are:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>“Stripchat tokens hack” and “unlimited tokens” sites are typically built to steal accounts, not to credit tokens.</li>
        <li>Fake generators usually end in survey loops, APK/profile downloads, or requests for your login and verification codes.</li>
        <li>Unknown APK files and iOS profiles can carry malware or spyware for iOS and Android devices.</li>
        <li>You should never share your password, payment details, or 2FA/recovery codes with any token website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="video-source">
        Source:
        <a href={VIDEO.watchUrl} rel="noopener nofollow">
          {VIDEO.name} — {VIDEO.publisherName} on YouTube
        </a>
        (published September 17, 2026). The written guide below was prepared
        independently by our editorial team.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
